<title>HONG KONG: Wharf seen seeking HK$3 bln loan - banker.</title>
<headline>Wharf seen seeking HK$3 bln loan - banker.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wharf (Holdings) Ltd is expected to seek HK$3 billion through a five-year syndicated loan to be launched on Wednesday, bankers said.</p>
<p>They said Chase Manhattan Asia, Standard Chartered Investment Banking and Hang Seng Bank Ltd were arranging the loan.</p>
<p>They gave no details of pricing.</p>
<p>Bankers said Wharf was one of the last of Hong Kong's blue chips to refinance, taking advantage of funding costs which have fallen by at least 20 basis points this year.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6371</p>
</text>
